  "description": string;
  /** What the operator can actually do. A POINTER, never a list of credentials. `turn_changed_nothing` names `run.worker.acp.env_passthrough` as the operator's channel and NEVER which variables belong in it: that field exists so a secret crossing into a worker is a declared act by the person who owns it. `turn_refused` branches on `auth_state`: signed out points at the agent's own login (via `wring doctor`, where the machine-aware routes live); logged in says a missing login is not the cause; unread or unreadable keeps the honest survey. Every branch names the worker log, and none names a credential variable. */
  "remedy": string;
  /** The ACP `stopReason` the agent reported for the turn — a FACT from the ledger, recorded and never obeyed. A turn claiming `end_turn` having written nothing is the shape a deprecated adapter's unauthenticated reply has. OPTIONAL since v2, and absent for `turn_refused`: a turn that was refused never reached a stop reason, and `"none"` or `"unknown"` written here would be an invented fact about a conversation that did not happen. */
  "stop_reason"?: string;
  /** How many files the turn wrote through the file seam. OPTIONAL since v2: present when a ledger survived the turn, absent when the failure came before there was one. Zero is what makes `turn_changed_nothing` apply; the number is recorded rather than the fact, so a reader sees what was counted. */
  "files_written"?: number;
  /** How many writes the file seam refused during the turn. OPTIONAL since v2, for `files_written`'s reason. Zero, likewise: a turn that was refused a write DID try to do something, and is a different ending with its own evidence. */
  "refusals"?: number;
  /** The agent's own last account of itself, if it gave one, carried verbatim BESIDE the description rather than parsed into it. Detection never reads this — F6's law: route on facts, hint on text, claim on neither — and the deprecated adapter's empty success is precisely why text cannot be trusted here. For `turn_refused` this is the agent's error message, and it is the one line that told a real operator what had gone wrong; it is scrubbed by the bundle's redactor on the way to disk like every other write. */
  "engine_words"?: string;
  /** What the agent's own auth surface said when the diagnosis was composed — a FACT read by `worker_auth.read` at the stop, never a guess from text. An OPEN string on the `wringer.loop.v2` `reason` precedent, so a new state costs no schema version; its known values are `logged_in` (the agent reports itself logged in — a missing login is not the cause), `logged_out` (the agent's own report of being signed out — the one answer that brings the login reading back), and `unknown` (the agent's auth surface could not be read, or answered in no shape this check trusts). Present only when the agent was ASKED: absent means nobody asked, which is different from any answer, and every record written before v3 is absent here. */
